server/.env
server/.aisstream.lock
# Cloudflare Pages local secrets for the landing function -- the local
# equivalent of .env, holding RESEND_API_KEY. Path-qualified to match
# server/.env above; the bare `.dev.vars` rule further down also covers it,
# and both are kept deliberately so removing either still leaves the key
# protected.
landing/.dev.vars
server/captures/
*.ndjson
*.jsonl

# Throwaway investigation tooling, never production code and never shipped.
server/tools/

**/public/tiles/*.pmtiles
# ...except VIS-9's Dover basemap, which SHIPS: it is the extract the
# hardcoded BASEMAP_AREAS.dover pmtilesUrl asks for, so committing it is
# what gives a fresh clone a coastline on the default area. 10,025,656
# bytes, z0-11. The broad rule above is deliberately kept so every other
# archive -- the rail Stockholm one and the prototypes' -- stays out.
!apps/display/public/tiles/dover-z11.pmtiles

# VIS-9 throwaway audit tooling (not production code)
vis9-audit/

# LANDING throwaway audit tooling (not production code)
landing-audit/

# LANDING/DEMO-2. Cloudflare Pages local development. These rules also exist
# on feat/landing-page, and are duplicated here because switching back to
# main leaves both directories behind in the working tree while the ignore
# rules go with the branch -- which left a file holding a live API key
# stageable on main.
.dev.vars
.wrangler/
